  "live_records": {
    "q-333701": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333701",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?",
      "worked_solution": "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
