    "q-334332": {
      "dom_id": "step-q334332",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?",
      "worked_solution": "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & -{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-334332-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ -{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & {e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\end{aligned}]",
